  "sourceNotes": [
    "All four GS papers have 100 scored items and no dropped/multiple answers. Official final key pages were visually verified for 2015 C, 2016 A, 2017 A and 2018 C. Explanations are editorial study notes, not UPSC explanations. Scoring remains 2 marks and a one-third penalty. Original scans for 2015/2018 are Series A and were matched by wording when checking the Series C transcriptions. The printed typo “Treasury bills offer are issued” in 2018 Q66 statement 3 is retained.",
    "Question wording, passages and option order are restored against original English scans. Answers use matching UPSC final keys; explanations are concise editorial study notes, not UPSC-provided explanations. 2015 C Q71 is ungraded and the remaining 79 items total 200 practice marks. No multiple accepted answers in either paper.",
    "All 160 final-key entries were visually checked on the original UPSC key pages. Both papers have 80 scoring items and no dropped or multiple accepted answers. Editorial explanations are original reasoning notes, not UPSC explanations. Figure crops are taken from the original 2018 Series A scan and were visually reviewed."
  ]
